  "result": "DIAGNOSTIC OVERHEAD CONFIRMED; CAUSALITY AND EXHAUSTION TIME NOT MEASURED",
  "source_findings": [
    "Old 0008 has no environment gate and permits up to 256 cache and 256 coroutine fprintf calls per host thread.",
    "After a logging budget is exhausted, its fprintf/heap/stack-base work returns early inside the logging helper, but call sites still evaluate stack-current getters and increment transaction IDs. The old budget does not remove hot-path diagnostic overhead.",
    "Cache write IDs advance for all MMU writes before bounds/invalid checks, whereas cache log budget advances only for printed calls. Turning diagnostics off must not change actual MMU behavior; opt-in trace-on retains this ID/invalid-write distinction.",
    "Coroutine log phases surround fiber swap. A caller-side budget check after fiber return must be fresh because intervening coroutine activity can exhaust the shared per-thread log budget."
  ],
  "timeline_limit": "Formal harness records UART at_ms, but diagnostics are only the final rolling 32768-character buffer with no per-line at_ms or guest timestamp. Therefore log256 proves exhaustion by evidence snapshot, not exhaustion before the first panic character.",
